          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Russian Industry</strong><br>\nMendeleev also contributed to the development of Russia's first oil refinery. He recognized the value of petroleum to the future of Russian industry and economy. His work included studies on the optimal balance of agricultural production, underscoring his diverse interests and impact on Russia's development.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nMendeleev passed away in 1907 in Saint Petersburg, Russia. By then, he had received recognition from scientific communities across Europe. His legacy is not just the discovery of the Periodic Law but also the methodology for scientific inquiry and classification that continued to influence chemistry and other sciences.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Recognition and Honors Posthumously</strong><br>\nAfter his death, Mendeleev's impact continued to grow. In 1955, element 101 was discovered and named mendelevium in his honor. His birth anniversary and work are celebrated in Russia and by chemists worldwide. Mendeleev remains a central figure in the study of chemistry, remembered for his foresight and contributions to the field.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
